%[text] # Exercise 3: Compress an AI Model for Deployment
%[text:tableOfContents]{"heading":"Table of Contents"}
%[text] Start the compression workflow with a trained network. The network performs speaker identification. For speaker recognition, x-vectors are extracted and fed into a separate classifier. Continuously monitor identification accuracy and recognition error rate throughout compression workflow.
%[text] ## 1. Analyze original model
%[text] Load the trained network. The network is a smaller variant (i.e. fewer layers and less filters) of the network from the example [Speaker Recognition Using x-vectors](https://uk.mathworks.com/help/deeplearning/ug/speaker-recognition-using-x-vectors.html).
load("netTrainedSmall.mat","net")
%[text] Load the data needed for training, validation and testing. The data is a subset of the dataset used in the example [Speaker Recognition Using x-vectors](https://uk.mathworks.com/help/deeplearning/ug/speaker-recognition-using-x-vectors.html). The data is already preprocessed, i.e. predictors are variable-length vector sequences containing 30 MFCC features per frame. Targets represent one of 251 speaker IDs.
data = load("trainDataSmall.mat",...
    "xTrain","tTrain","xValidation","tValidation","xTest","tTest",...
    "xEnroll","tEnroll","xDET","tDET","afe","classes");
%[text] Reduce noise from sequence truncation or padding during testing by sorting the sequences by length, so that each mini-batch contains sequences of similar length.
[data.xTest,data.tTest] = sortbySequenceLength(data.xTest,data.tTest);
[data.xEnroll,data.tEnroll] = sortbySequenceLength(data.xEnroll,data.tEnroll);
[data.xDET,data.tDET] = sortbySequenceLength(data.xDET,data.tDET);
%[text] To enable shuffling of the data during fine-tuning while avoiding truncation/padding of sequences, split the training and validation sequences into chunks of sequence length 100.
seqChunkLength = 100;
[xTrainChunks,tTrainChunks] = helperChunkSequences(data.xTrain,data.tTrain,seqChunkLength);
[xValidationChunks,tValidationChunks] = helperChunkSequences(data.xValidation,data.tValidation,seqChunkLength);
%%
%[text] Compute accuracy for speaker identification on the test data set. 
mbsize = 256;
accuracyOriginal = testnet(net,data.xTest,data.tTest,"accuracy",... %[output:group:4ada758b] %[output:41d783aa]
    MiniBatchSize = mbsize, ... %[output:41d783aa]
    SequenceLength="shortest") %[output:group:4ada758b] %[output:41d783aa]
%%
%[text] Compute the equal error rate for speaker verification. 
eerOriginal = evaluateAndPlotDetectionError(net,data); %[output:6c84a691] %[output:18d29420]
%%
%[text] ## 2. Analyze network for compression
%[text] Determine which compression techniques are available and applicable to the network.
%[text] Get a sense of the parameter memory needed to store the network and how much compression can maximally reduce the memory usage.
%[text] Open the network in Deep Network Designer and **click on the "Compression Analysis" button** in the toolstrip.
deepNetworkDesigner(net)
%[text] ![](text:image:7fd1)
%%
%[text] ## 3. Compress the network using pruning
%[text] The [`compressNetworkUsingTaylorPruning`](https://www.mathworks.com/help/deeplearning/ref/compressnetworkusingtaylorpruning.html) (since R2026a) function prunes a network iteratively by repeating these steps:
%[text] 1. Compute the importance score of each prunable filter using Taylor approximation.
%[text] 2. Prune the least important filters.
%[text] 3. Fine-tune the pruned network. \
%[text] Specify the training options for the fine-tuning step. Use the same options that were used to train the original network, but use fewer training epochs. The network does not need to be trained from scratch, so you need fewer training epochs to retrain it.
numIterPerEpoch = floor(numel(xTrainChunks)/mbsize);
options = trainingOptions("adam", ...
    MaxEpochs = 4, ...
    MiniBatchSize = mbsize, ...
    Metrics = "accuracy", ...
    OutputNetwork = "best-validation", ...
    ObjectiveMetricName = "accuracy",...
    ValidationFrequency = numIterPerEpoch/2,...
    ValidationPatience = 3,...
    ValidationData = {xValidationChunks,tValidationChunks}, ...
    Shuffle = "every-epoch", ...
    SequenceLength = "shortest");
%[text] Instead of maximally pruning the network, only prune the network so much that accuracy is still roughly maintained. 
valAccuracyThresh = testnet(net,xValidationChunks,tValidationChunks,"accuracy") - 2;
%[text] Prune the network (this can take 10-15 minutes) or load the pruned network from file.
[netPruned,pruningInfo] = compressNetworkUsingTaylorPruning(net,... %[output:group:90f40262] %[output:20ffce67] %[output:0e9457ff]
    xTrainChunks,tTrainChunks,"crossentropy",options,... %[output:20ffce67] %[output:0e9457ff]
    LearnablesReductionIncrement=0.025,... %[output:20ffce67] %[output:0e9457ff]
    ValidationThreshold=valAccuracyThresh); %[output:20ffce67] %[output:0e9457ff]
% save("prunedNet.mat","netPruned","pruningInfo") %[output:group:90f40262]
%%
%[text] ### Evaluate pruned network
%[text] Explore which layers were pruned by the software. 
compareNetworkStructure(net,netPruned) %[output:1b079d30]
%[text] Compute the accuracy for speaker identification on the test data set. 
accuracyPruned = testnet(netPruned,data.xTest,data.tTest,"accuracy",... %[output:group:664e9f5b] %[output:2da1268b]
    SequenceLength="shortest") %[output:group:664e9f5b] %[output:2da1268b]
%[text] Compute the equal error rate for speaker verification. Reduce the number of dimensions used of PLDA if warnings occur.
rng(1)
eerPruned = evaluateAndPlotDetectionError(netPruned,data,PLDANumDimensions=145); %[output:77334577] %[output:90d58be2]
%%
%[text] ## 4. Compress the network using projection
% load("prunedNet.mat","netPruned","pruningInfo")
%[text] Projection allows you to convert large layers with many learnables to one or more smaller layers with fewer total learnable parameters.
%[text] The [`compressNetworkUsingProjection`](https://www.mathworks.com/help/deeplearning/ref/compressnetworkusingprojection.html) function applies principal component analysis (PCA) to the training data to identify the subspace of learnables that result in the highest variance in neuron activations. Compute the `neuronPCA` analysis first in order to more efficiently explore different compression levels. 
npca = neuronPCA(netPruned,xValidationChunks) %[output:19dec815] %[output:70cb6ed2]
%%
%[text] The fully connected layers and outputs of the last conv layer were not pruned and still have lots of potential for structural compression via projection.
%[text] Explore how many principal components are required at the layer boundaries to maintain the desired variance in the neuron activation space. 
explainedVar = 98; %[control:editfield:0436]{"position":[16,18]}
summarizeExplainedVariance(npca,explainedVar) %[output:715e7cc2]
%%
%[text] ### Projection trade-off analysis
%[text] Try out various compression amounts (between 20% and 80% learnables reduction) without retraining.
figure %[output:14f43a4a]
h = animatedline(LineStyle="--",Marker="o"); %[output:14f43a4a]
xlabel("Learnables Reduction (%)") %[output:14f43a4a]
ylabel("Accuracy (%)") %[output:14f43a4a]
title("Validation Accuracy of Projected Networks") %[output:14f43a4a]

for reductionGoal = 0.2:0.05:0.8
    [netProjected,info] = compressNetworkUsingProjection(netPruned,npca,...
        LearnablesReductionGoal=reductionGoal,VerbosityLevel="off");

    learnablesReduction = 100*info.LearnablesReduction;
    accuracyProjected =  testnet(netProjected,xValidationChunks,tValidationChunks,"accuracy",MiniBatchSize=mbsize);

    addpoints(h,learnablesReduction,accuracyProjected) %[output:14f43a4a]
    drawnow
end
grid on %[output:14f43a4a]
%%
%[text] Based on the trade-off analysis, choose the desired compression level and further retrain the projected network.
preferredReduction = 0.5; %[control:editfield:3a30]{"position":[22,25]}
[netProjected, projectionInfo] = compressNetworkUsingProjection(netPruned,npca,LearnablesReductionGoal=preferredReduction); %[output:3d18be17]
projectionInfo %[output:0fec1446]
%[text] Use analyzeNetwork to explore how much each layer was compressed using projection (see last column).
analyzeNetwork(netProjected)
%[text] Retrain the projected network to improve accuracy,
options.MaxEpochs = 10;
options.Plots = "training-progress";
options.ValidationPatience = 3;
netProjected = trainnet(xTrainChunks,tTrainChunks,netProjected,"crossentropy",options); %[output:34284f04] %[output:62d85c58]
% save("projectedNet.mat","netProjected","projectionInfo")
%%
%[text] ### Evaluate the pruned+projected network
%[text] Load the projected network from file to avoid rerunning the projection step above.
% load("projectedNet.mat","netProjected","projectionInfo")
%[text] Compute the accuracy for speaker identification on the test data set.
accuracyProjected = testnet(netProjected,data.xTest,data.tTest,"accuracy",... %[output:group:0848b364] %[output:0ba41d92]
    SequenceLength="shortest") %[output:group:0848b364] %[output:0ba41d92]
%[text] Compute the equal error rate for speaker verification. Speaker verification extracts embedding vectors from the first fully connected layer and performs LDA on these output activations. Since the fully connected layer was projected, it already maps the input activations down to a lower-dimension subspace. 
embedLayer = getLayer(netProjected,"fc_1") %[output:13fb03d4]
%[text] Use this lower dimensional representation of the x-vectors directly for the LDA+PLDA analysis. Unpack the projected layers first to get access to this intermediate representation (i.e. the output from `"fc_1_proj_in"`). Adjust the number of eigenvectors for LDA analysis to be smaller or equal to the number of output channels from layer `"fc_1_proj_in".`
netProjectedUnpacked = unpackProjectedLayers(netProjected);
eerProjected = evaluateAndPlotDetectionError(netProjectedUnpacked,data,... %[output:group:88b1106c] %[output:1f8a940a] %[output:77b142e2]
    EmbeddingLayer="fc_1_proj_in",LDANumEigenvectors=embedLayer.OutputProjectorSize); %[output:group:88b1106c] %[output:1f8a940a] %[output:77b142e2]
%%
%[text] ## 5. Compress the network using quantization
%[text] Quantize the network either with the Deep Network Quantizer app (`deepNetworkQuantizer`) or in the command-line via the following steps:
%[text] 1. Create the quantizer object. Use the "MATLAB" execution environment to later generate library-free C code
%[text] 2. Prepare the network for quantization to improve accuracy and improve efficiency
%[text] 3. Calibrate the network to collect the dynamic ranges of the weights/activations
%[text] 4. Quantize the network  \
quantObj = dlquantizer(netProjected,ExecutionEnvironment="MATLAB");
prepareNetwork(quantObj)
calibrate(quantObj,xValidationChunks,UseGPU="off");
netQuantized = quantize(quantObj,"ExponentScheme","Histogram");
%[text] Use the `quantizationDetails` function to inspect which parameters/layers were quantized and how.
qDetails = quantizationDetails(netQuantized) %[output:2e3dac07]
% save("quantizedNet.mat","netQuantized","quantObj")
%%
%[text] ### Evaluate pruned+projected+quantized network
%[text] Load the quantized network from file to avoid rerunning the quantization step above.
% load("quantizedNet.mat","netQuantized")
%[text] Compute the accuracy for speaker identification on the test data set.
accuracyQuantized = testnet(netQuantized,data.xTest,data.tTest,"accuracy",... %[output:group:3350baa9] %[output:7df0db84]
    SequenceLength="shortest") %[output:group:3350baa9] %[output:7df0db84]
%[text] Speaker verification 
rng(1)
eerQuantized = evaluateAndPlotDetectionError(netQuantized,data,... %[output:group:6b23bca0] %[output:94b2a8f2] %[output:4bb493bf]
    EmbeddingLayer="fc_1_proj_in",LDANumEigenvectors=embedLayer.OutputProjectorSize); %[output:group:6b23bca0] %[output:94b2a8f2] %[output:4bb493bf]
%%
%[text] ## 6. Summarize effect of combining multiple compression techniques
%[text] Compare the memory needs after each compression step. Only count layers that are required to compute the x-vectors used for speaker verification.
%[text] Separate the network memory into the part needed for speaker verification and the rest that is also needed for speaker identification.
memory = [learnablesMemoryInMB(net,"fc_1")
    learnablesMemoryInMB(netPruned,"fc_1")
    learnablesMemoryInMB(netProjectedUnpacked,"fc_1_proj_in")
    learnablesMemoryInMB(netQuantized,"fc_1_proj_in")];
memory(:,2) = [
    learnablesMemoryInMB(net)
    learnablesMemoryInMB(netPruned)
    learnablesMemoryInMB(netProjectedUnpacked   )
    learnablesMemoryInMB(netQuantized)] - memory(:,1);
%[text] Gather accuracy and error rates. 
accuracy = [accuracyOriginal, accuracyPruned, accuracyProjected, accuracyQuantized];
equalErrorRate = [eerOriginal, eerPruned, eerProjected, eerQuantized];
%[text] Plot a bar chart to compare speaker identification accuracy, equal error rate for speaker verification and the memory of the networks.
figure %[output:1d5f47c3]
tiledlayout("vertical") %[output:1d5f47c3]
t1 = nexttile; %[output:1d5f47c3]
b1 = bar(t1,accuracy); %[output:1d5f47c3]
x = b1.XData;
for i = 1:length(accuracy)
    text(x(i), accuracy(i), num2str(accuracy(i)), ... %[output:1d5f47c3]
        'HorizontalAlignment', 'center', ... %[output:1d5f47c3]
        'VerticalAlignment', 'bottom'); %[output:1d5f47c3]
end
title(t1,"Accuracy") %[output:1d5f47c3]
xticklabels(["Original" "Pruned" "Projected" "Quantized"]) %[output:1d5f47c3]
ylim([0,1.2*max(accuracy)]) %[output:1d5f47c3]

t2 = nexttile; %[output:1d5f47c3]
b2 = bar(t2,equalErrorRate); %[output:1d5f47c3]
x = b2.XData;
for i = 1:length(equalErrorRate)
    text(x(i), equalErrorRate(i), num2str(equalErrorRate(i)), ... %[output:1d5f47c3]
        'HorizontalAlignment', 'center', ... %[output:1d5f47c3]
        'VerticalAlignment', 'bottom'); %[output:1d5f47c3]
end
title(t2,"Equal Error Rate") %[output:1d5f47c3]
xticklabels(["Original" "Pruned" "Projected" "Quantized"]) %[output:1d5f47c3]
ylim([0,1.2*max(equalErrorRate)]) %[output:1d5f47c3]

t3 = nexttile; %[output:1d5f47c3]
b3 = bar(t3,memory,'stacked'); %[output:1d5f47c3]
title(t3,"Memory (MB)") %[output:1d5f47c3]
xticklabels(["Original" "Pruned" "Projected" "Quantized"]) %[output:1d5f47c3]
ylim([0,1.2*max(sum(memory,2))]) %[output:1d5f47c3]
%%
%[text] ## Helper Functions
%[text] Sort vector sequences by sequence length
function [xData,tData] = sortbySequenceLength(xData,tData)
seqLen = cellfun(@(x)size(x,1),xData);
[~,idx] = sort(seqLen);
xData = xData(idx);
tData = tData(idx);
end
%[text] Compare the structure (i.e. number of learnables and number of channels) of two networks.
function T = compareNetworkStructure(netOrig,netCompr)
analysisOrig = analyzeNetwork(netOrig,Plots="none").LayerInfo;
analysisCompr = analyzeNetwork(netCompr,Plots="none").LayerInfo;
T = analysisOrig(:,["Name","Type"]);
T.LearnablesOriginal = analysisOrig.NumLearnables;
T.LearnablesReduction = 1-analysisCompr.NumLearnables./analysisOrig.NumLearnables;
T.NumOutputChannelsOriginal = cellfun(@(sz,fmt)sz(char(fmt)=='C'),analysisOrig.ActivationSizes,analysisOrig.ActivationFormats);
T.NumOutputChannelsCompressed = cellfun(@(sz,fmt)sz(char(fmt)=='C'),analysisCompr.ActivationSizes,analysisCompr.ActivationFormats);
% Don't compare layers without learnable parameters
T(T.LearnablesOriginal==0,:)=[];
end
%[text] Compute the memory needed to store learnable parameters.
function mem = learnablesMemoryInMB(net,lastLayer)
arguments
    net
    lastLayer = string.empty
end
layerInfo = estimateNetworkMetrics(net);
if isempty(lastLayer)
    rowIdx = 1:height(layerInfo);
else
    allNames = {net.Layers.Name};
    namesOfInterest = allNames(1:find(ismember(allNames,lastLayer)));
    rowIdx = ismember(layerInfo.LayerName,namesOfInterest);
end
mem = sum(layerInfo{rowIdx,"ParameterMemory (MB)"});
end
%[text] Perform speaker verification and evaluate the error rate for a test set.
function [eerPLDA,projMat,plda] = evaluateAndPlotDetectionError(net,data,opts)
arguments
    net dlnetwork
    data
    opts.MiniBatchSize = 256
    opts.EmbeddingLayer = "fc_1"
    opts.LDANumEigenvectors = 150
    opts.PLDANumIterations = 3
    opts.PLDANumDimensions = 150
end

%% Train LDA projection matrix and PLDA system 
disp("Compute x-vectors and LDA for training data using "+opts.LDANumEigenvectors+" eigen vectors")
xvecsTrain = minibatchpredict(net,data.xTrain, ...
    Outputs=opts.EmbeddingLayer, ...
    MiniBatchSize=opts.MiniBatchSize, ...
    SequenceLength="shortest");
xvecsTrain = xvecsTrain';

% Create a linear discriminant analysis (LDA) projection matrix to reduce
% the dimensionality of the x-vectors.
projMat = helperTrainProjectionMatrix(xvecsTrain,data.tTrain,opts.LDANumEigenvectors);

% Apply the LDA projection matrix to the x-vectors.
xvecsTrainP = projMat*xvecsTrain;

% Train a PLDA model to perform scoring.
numDimensions = min(opts.LDANumEigenvectors,opts.PLDANumDimensions);
disp("Train PLDA model using "+numDimensions+" dimensions")
plda = helperTrainPLDA(xvecsTrainP,data.tTrain,opts.PLDANumIterations,numDimensions);

%% Evaluate x-vector system
disp("Create template x-vectors per speaker using held-out enrollment data set")

% Extract x-vectors from the held-out enrollment data set.
xvecsEnroll = minibatchpredict(net,data.xEnroll, ...
    MiniBatchSize=1, ...
    Outputs=opts.EmbeddingLayer);
xvecsEnrollP = projMat*xvecsEnroll';

% Create template x-vectors for each speaker by averaging the x-vectors of individual speakers across enrollment files.
uniqueLabels = unique(data.tEnroll);
enrollmentTable = cell2table(cell(0,2),VariableNames=["xvector","NumSamples"]);
for ii = 1:numel(uniqueLabels)
    idx = uniqueLabels(ii)==data.tEnroll;
    wLocalMean = mean(xvecsEnrollP(:,idx),2);
    localTable = table({wLocalMean},(sum(idx)), ...
        VariableNames=["xvector","NumSamples"], ...
        RowNames=string(uniqueLabels(ii)));
    enrollmentTable = [enrollmentTable;localTable]; %#ok<AGROW>
end

%% Detection Error Tradeoff
% Speaker verification systems require you to set a threshold that balances
% the probability of a false acceptance (FA) and the probability of a false
% rejection (FR), according to the requirements of your application. To
% determine the threshold that meets your FA/FR requirements, evaluate the
% detection error tradeoff of the system.
disp("Determine detection error trade-off")
xvecsDET = minibatchpredict(net,data.xDET, ...
    MiniBatchSize=1, ...
    Outputs=opts.EmbeddingLayer);
xvecsDET = xvecsDET';
xvecsDETP = projMat*xvecsDET;

detTable = helperDetectionErrorTradeoff(xvecsDETP,data.tDET,enrollmentTable,plda);

% Plot the results of the detection error tradeoff evaluation for both PLDA
% scoring and cosine similarity scoring (CSS).
figure
tiledlayout(1,2);

nexttile
plot(detTable.PLDA.Threshold,detTable.PLDA.FAR, ...
    detTable.PLDA.Threshold,detTable.PLDA.FRR)
eerPLDA = helperEqualErrorRate(detTable.PLDA);
title(["Speaker Verification","Detection Error Tradeoff","PLDA Scoring","Equal Error Rate = " + eerPLDA]);
xlabel("Threshold")
ylabel("Error Rate")
legend(["FAR","FRR"])

nexttile
plot(detTable.CSS.Threshold,detTable.CSS.FAR, ...
    detTable.CSS.Threshold,detTable.CSS.FRR)
eerCSS = helperEqualErrorRate(detTable.CSS);
title(["Speaker Verification","Detection Error Tradeoff","Cosine Similarity Scoring","Equal Error Rate = " + eerCSS]);
xlabel("Threshold")
ylabel("Error Rate")
legend(["FAR","FRR"])
end

